course: dictionary
lesson: 1793
title: Meet the clockmaker
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A clockmaker is a person who makes and repairs clocks. You can often work out a word by looking at its parts. Clock is the thing, and maker is someone who makes things, so a clockmaker makes clocks.
explain: Context gives more clues. «A grandfather clock counts the swings of its pendulum, and clockmakers move a little weight up or down to make it run faster or slower.» The sentence tells you clockmakers adjust clocks so they keep the right time.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The clockmaker repaired the old grandfather clock.» If you put in a baker or a painter instead, the sentence stops making sense, so the clue points to someone who works with clocks.
fact: A clockmaker is a person who makes and repairs clocks.
fact: Clockmaker is a noun. The plural is clockmakers.
fact: A «pendulum» is a weight that swings to and fro, and it helps a clock keep time.
fact: On a Roman clock, I = 1, V = 5 and X = 10, so «IX» is 9 and «XII» is 12.
fact: Clockmakers once liked to show 4 as «IIII» on some clocks, which shows that people made their own choices about how clocks looked.
exercise: «The clockmaker mended the broken clock.» What is a clockmaker? | *A person who makes and repairs clocks | A tall tower on a church | A person who sells cakes | A tool for cutting wood
exercise: «A grandfather clock counts the swings of its pendulum.» What does the pendulum do? | It stays still | It sings | *It swings | It melts
exercise: On some clocks, «IIII» is used for 4. What does IIII stand for? | *4 | 5 | 14 | 3
test: «Clockmakers move a little weight up or down.» Why would a clockmaker do this? | To hang the clock on a wall | To make the clock louder | *To make the clock run faster or slower | To change the colour of the clock
test: Which job is a clockmaker's job? | Baking bread | Driving a bus | *Repairing a clock that has stopped | Painting pictures of the sea
exam: A clockmaker is best described as | *Someone who makes and repairs clocks | Someone who grows vegetables | Someone who paints pictures | Someone who drives a bus
